#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198020 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198378 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b46ce4-cfe0-5da6-bc91-65ae8c544393" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Through a Surface as a Double Integral"}] :question/id #uuid "9a1112c0-db94-5572-ba53-b78116b7c273" :question/math-academy-id "e-12355" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) =\\left\\langle x+y,\\: x-y,\\: xyz \\right\\rangle, \\quad \\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle u^2,\\: v^2 ,\\: 1 \\right\\rangle, \\quad (u,v)\\in D\\subset \\mathbb{R}^2.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $\\mathbf F$ across $S$ with respect to $\\mathbf{n}$ is given by\n\n![](images/d7/d7b8d89cae048a9cd5e04299bebdcb3a5d5d21ac6d5a31c48482aa00ca71517c.svg)\n\nwhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n} \\,\\textrm{d}S\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\cdot (\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v) \\,\\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 2v & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,4uv⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x+y,\\,x-y,\\,xyz⟩{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y={v}^{2}\\,z=1} \\\\  & =⟨{u}^{2}+{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}{v}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and $\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨{u}^{2}+{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}{v}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,0,\\,4uv⟩ \\\\  & =({u}^{2}+{v}^{2})\\cdot 0+({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\cdot 0+{u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\cdot 4uv \\\\  & =4{u}^{3}{v}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,4{u}^{3}{v}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198022 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198380 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/id #uuid "0364a11f-e567-517e-acf2-471708dbdc0a" :question/math-academy-id "e-12358" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\left\\langle z, \\: x, \\: y \\right\\rangle \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle 1+2u+v, \\: u+v, \\: u-v \\right\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $0 \\leq u \\leq 2$ and $0 \\leq v \\leq 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n} \\,\\textrm{d}S\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\cdot (\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v) \\,\\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1+2u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1+2u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨z,\\,x,\\,y⟩|}_{x=1+2u+v\\,y=u+v\\,z=u-v} \\\\  & =⟨u-v,\\,1+2u+v,\\,u+v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and $\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u-v,\\,1+2u+v,\\,u+v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,\\,3,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(u-v)\\cdot (-2)+(1+2u+v)\\cdot 3+(u+v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2u+2v+3+6u+3v+u+v \\\\  & =5u+6v+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,x,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5u+6v+3)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(5u+6v+3)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[5uv+3{v}^{2}+3v]_{v=0}^{v=1}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(5u+6)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={[\\frac{5}{2}{u}^{2}+6u]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =10+12 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198585 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198378 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b46ce4-cfe0-5da6-bc91-65ae8c544393" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Through a Surface as a Double Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "194750cf-4b33-5153-97c1-bd1b0f21c3c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u{v}^{3}+8{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275713} {:answer/id #uuid "30772c46-8461-5daa-94aa-ff5b8a754f75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275909} {:answer/id #uuid "45100deb-1ec8-5bbb-b0b4-3c26c5616332" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u{v}^{3}+4{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276086} {:answer/id #uuid "45e6001c-4deb-5a8c-b01f-01531e4489d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4u{v}^{3}+2{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276094} {:answer/id #uuid "936bab95-9822-587d-80ac-54eded632448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276811}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "936bab95-9822-587d-80ac-54eded632448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276811} :answer-field/id #uuid "f81d9840-6037-5557-81d1-599235b0ea5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278161}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9fcf8673-a62b-588a-8020-ca78007689b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-160840" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨2x+y,\\,2z,\\,y+z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨-{u}^{2},\\,2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,{v}^{2}⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨8uv,\\,4uv,\\,4uv⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨8uv,\\,4uv,\\,4uv⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨2x+y,\\,2z,\\,y+z⟩{|}_{x=-{u}^{2}\\,y=2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨2(-{u}^{2})+(2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}),\\,2({v}^{2}),\\,(2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2})+{v}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{v}^{2},\\,2{v}^{2},\\,2{u}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨-{v}^{2},\\,2{v}^{2},\\,2{u}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨8uv,\\,4uv,\\,4uv⟩ \\\\  & =(-{v}^{2})\\cdot 8uv+2{v}^{2}\\cdot 4uv+2{u}^{2}\\cdot 4uv \\\\  & =-8u{v}^{3}+8u{v}^{3}+8{u}^{3}v \\\\  & =8{u}^{3}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,8{u}^{3}v\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198592 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198380 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11be498b-977a-5f13-82a0-b8754dc5bd8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275636} {:answer/id #uuid "8b18291e-b1ba-55db-80ed-c83639075677" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276737} {:answer/id #uuid "bc028827-be53-5841-a899-754876ec3402" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277150} {:answer/id #uuid "d4a0b90a-2bd6-5552-afc1-f83bdcf172c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277350} {:answer/id #uuid "eb4662bc-b4e4-5fee-98bc-64e89c915aa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b18291e-b1ba-55db-80ed-c83639075677" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276737} :answer-field/id #uuid "42073408-3ed9-5a4e-b4da-76268342b625" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e6b5a3a2-513f-5721-bf54-260cfc8a8f5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-160886" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨2x,\\,\\frac{xz}{3}-2y,\\,2z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2u-1,\\,uv,\\,3v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨3v,\\,-6,\\,2u⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨3v,\\,-6,\\,2u⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨2x,\\,\\frac{xz}{3}-2y,\\,2z⟩|}_{x=2u-1\\,y=uv\\,z=3v} \\\\  & =⟨2(2u-1),\\,\\frac{(2u-1)(3v)}{3}-2uv,\\,2(3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4u-2,\\,-v,\\,6v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨4u-2,\\,-v,\\,6v⟩\\cdot ⟨3v,\\,-6,\\,2u⟩ \\\\  & =(4u-2)\\cdot 3v+(-v)\\cdot (-6)+6v\\cdot 2u \\\\  & =12uv-6v+6v+12uv \\\\  & =24uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨2x,\\,\\frac{xz}{3}-2y,\\,2z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}24uv\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}24uv\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}[12{u}^{2}v]_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}12v\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =[6{v}^{2}]_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =6({2}^{2}-(-1)^{2}) \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278446 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198378 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b46ce4-cfe0-5da6-bc91-65ae8c544393" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Through a Surface as a Double Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1761d05c-b47b-569a-b7b6-4ed471f6dadf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275697} {:answer/id #uuid "40392ee9-b3f1-5009-bd69-fc1a719298c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{3}v+u{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276036} {:answer/id #uuid "66d47ff6-4d2f-51dd-a0bd-fe3a8ddbdd70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{u}^{3}v-2u{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276396} {:answer/id #uuid "d6d10ecc-5a2a-5169-bb03-eaafe2a1f99a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{u}^{2}{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277369} {:answer/id #uuid "da347498-a4dc-5e22-9cb1-7985c24efdcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}v-2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+u{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1761d05c-b47b-569a-b7b6-4ed471f6dadf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275697} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9c299fe-08c9-5f88-b42b-ca47c7784874" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278018}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a99addda-c910-54da-a8cb-ae3a5ce916a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161249" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨2x,\\,2y,\\,z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,-uv,\\,{v}^{2}⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2{v}^{2},\\,-4uv,\\,-2{u}^{2}⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2{v}^{2},\\,-4uv,\\,-2{u}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨2x,\\,2y,\\,z⟩{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=-uv\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨2{u}^{2},\\,-2uv,\\,{v}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨2{u}^{2},\\,-2uv,\\,{v}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨-2{v}^{2},\\,-4uv,\\,-2{u}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =2{u}^{2}\\cdot (-2{v}^{2})+(-2uv)\\cdot (-4uv)+{v}^{2}\\cdot (-2{u}^{2}) \\\\  & =-4{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+8{u}^{2}{v}^{2}-2{u}^{2}{v}^{2} \\\\  & =2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398507 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198378 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b46ce4-cfe0-5da6-bc91-65ae8c544393" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Through a Surface as a Double Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d89472a-c8a6-58ee-ad06-702bb85242bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{u}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398509} {:answer/id #uuid "6ceed292-fdb3-5c81-a5ef-e21d4577bafc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\operatorname{cos}⁡v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398510} {:answer/id #uuid "2e773ddf-4b3c-5bc1-b538-c1702b36529f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\operatorname{cos}⁡v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398511} {:answer/id #uuid "06d6268a-1fe9-5430-934f-527eb0153af9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5{u}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398512} {:answer/id #uuid "c1b5545b-f437-5265-821f-6ea217aea603" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06d6268a-1fe9-5430-934f-527eb0153af9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5{u}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398512} :answer-field/id #uuid "f48bed04-e645-581d-90b2-d43b8caed324" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398508}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "50f21d4c-115f-5f6b-a6fe-50fa77f7169e" :question/math-academy-id "q-161251" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨3x,\\,3y,\\,z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{u}^{2}⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨3x,\\,3y,\\,z⟩{|}_{x=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\,y=u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\,z={u}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{u}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{u}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u⟩ \\\\  & =3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\cdot (-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)+3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\cdot (-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)+{u}^{2}\\cdot u \\\\  & =-6{u}^{3}({cos}^{2}⁡v+{sin}^{2}⁡v)+{u}^{3} \\\\  & =-5{u}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,-5{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198380 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c4ed277-51d3-5190-9f15-e73dd884cf47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434819} {:answer/id #uuid "471dabbc-d133-52dc-b559-394801c709a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434821} {:answer/id #uuid "777af6b2-9aef-5099-aac7-98b1ec37120e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434822} {:answer/id #uuid "8a1f231c-84b6-5409-b4c5-4c9196b18b4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434823} {:answer/id #uuid "de47629f-21da-52b1-941b-ae2f3625cecc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c4ed277-51d3-5190-9f15-e73dd884cf47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434819} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a1a0c12-6b57-5589-b4e1-416cdc457a68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434828}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f5815497-10bb-5d31-b1ef-c78b6eb79a17" :question/math-academy-id "q-161259" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨x,\\,y,\\,-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,v-u,\\,uv⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 0,\\,0\\le v\\le 1\\}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-u-v,\\,v-u,\\,2⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-u-v,\\,v-u,\\,2⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨x,\\,y,\\,-z⟩|}_{x=u+v\\,y=v-u\\,z=uv} \\\\  & =⟨u+v,\\,v-u,\\,-uv⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u+v,\\,v-u,\\,-uv⟩\\cdot ⟨-u-v,\\,v-u,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =(u+v)\\cdot (-u-v)+(v-u)\\cdot (v-u)+(-uv)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-{u}^{2}-2uv-{v}^{2}+{v}^{2}-2uv+{u}^{2}-2uv \\\\  & =-6uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x,\\,y,\\,-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-6uv)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-6{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}uv\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =-6{\\int }_{0}^{1}v\\,\\text{d}v{\\int }_{-2}^{0}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-6\\cdot [\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}]_{0}^{1}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}]}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278450 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198380 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23825e40-ec53-5f67-9638-35d121d51307" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275793} {:answer/id #uuid "5ec69f15-fbed-5296-9952-1dc103047426" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276325} {:answer/id #uuid "98e6e4b9-4435-58e2-9d7a-b732cdd0ce08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276849} {:answer/id #uuid "d47ba56f-6b65-598d-b6f5-90728d0382b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277348} {:answer/id #uuid "ebed3c1d-caab-55c6-88ae-97fc928a3dae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ec69f15-fbed-5296-9952-1dc103047426" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276325} :answer-field/id #uuid "20c0bba0-07fc-5c71-ba73-fcc312a83f3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277781}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c5de597f-04b0-56f5-aa9e-d79ce26e7706" :question/math-academy-id "q-161263" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨3,\\,z,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,v,\\,uv⟩\n$$\n\nfor $-1\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & v \\\\ 0 & 1 & u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & v \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & v \\\\ 0 & u\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-v,\\,-2{u}^{2},\\,2u⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨3,\\,z,\\,y⟩|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=v\\,z=uv} \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,uv,\\,v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3,\\,uv,\\,v⟩\\cdot ⟨-v,\\,-2{u}^{2},\\,2u⟩ \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-v)+uv\\cdot (-2{u}^{2})+v\\cdot 2u \\\\  & =-3v-2{u}^{3}v+2uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨3,\\,z,\\,y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-3v-2{u}^{3}v+2uv)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-3v-2{u}^{3}v+2uv)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-3uv-\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{4}v+{u}^{2}v]}_{u=-1}^{u=1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-6v)\\text{d}v \\\\  & =[-3{v}^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278459 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198380 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "355bef10-0b8c-5536-a445-f01d12172fb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275953} {:answer/id #uuid "59ce5885-1e3d-5f19-ba38-dbb31ab5b6a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276282} {:answer/id #uuid "638c8aa6-4abb-5caf-80fe-7e02a183ce5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276379} {:answer/id #uuid "821420d2-3a8a-52ab-bf19-2fe3c2fc1b2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276652} {:answer/id #uuid "c99962ef-c495-5547-948d-fcb7faccda71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277268}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c99962ef-c495-5547-948d-fcb7faccda71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277268} :answer-field/id #uuid "c470c898-ccdc-5a03-914c-a796d495fee6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278070}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5f5f7b83-0f5c-511f-9e98-a4ae85732cc3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161278" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨-x-z,\\,x-y,\\,-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,v-u,\\,-v⟩\n$$\n\nfor $-1\\le u\\le 0$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨-x-z,\\,x-y,\\,-z⟩|}_{x=u+v\\,y=v-u\\,z=-v} \\\\  & =⟨-(u+v)-(-v),\\,u+v-(v-u),\\,-(-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-u,\\,2u,\\,v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨-u,\\,2u,\\,v⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,1,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =(-u)\\cdot 1+2u\\cdot 1+v\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-u+2u+2v \\\\  & =u+2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨-x-z,\\,x-y,\\,-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(u+2v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(u+2v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}[uv+{v}^{2}]_{v=0}^{v=1}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(u+1)\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}+u]}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278470 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198378 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b46ce4-cfe0-5da6-bc91-65ae8c544393" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Through a Surface as a Double Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e4065be-6410-5ccf-b764-e323b3954972" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275595} {:answer/id #uuid "996e1145-cf3a-5420-96fd-aafd97d1eb20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276855} {:answer/id #uuid "9f1089df-e42d-5caa-8e67-1152d56ad3b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276907} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e32ea5-a6f3-52a4-b8ec-13ac55fa6f7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277004} {:answer/id #uuid "dedf319d-2d9f-52cc-bda0-79efe3637268" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f1089df-e42d-5caa-8e67-1152d56ad3b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276907} :answer-field/id #uuid "e799dfb7-bba2-57d2-9a73-5392e0c83466" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278129}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a2d1066e-0b79-5532-9ae3-4e710fbc5bc4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161303" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,{u}^{2}+2v,\\,{u}^{3}+3v⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}a{u}^{2}+bu+c\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}+2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{3}+3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2u,\\,3{u}^{2}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}+2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{3}+3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2,\\,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2u & 3{u}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}2u & 3{u}^{2} \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3{u}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2u \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6u-6{u}^{2},\\,3{u}^{2}-3,\\,2-2u⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩{|}_{x=u+v\\,y={u}^{2}+2v\\,z={u}^{3}+3v} \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨6u-6{u}^{2},\\,3{u}^{2}-3,\\,2-2u⟩ \\\\  & =1\\cdot (6u-6{u}^{2})+0\\cdot (3{u}^{2}-3)+2\\cdot (2-2u) \\\\  & =6u-6{u}^{2}+4-4u \\\\  & =-6{u}^{2}+2u+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-6)\\cdot {u}^{2}+2\\cdot u+4\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=-6+2+4=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278507 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198378 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b46ce4-cfe0-5da6-bc91-65ae8c544393" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Through a Surface as a Double Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d1c9dba-209f-56b2-8f1b-b1d0237d58ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275746} {:answer/id #uuid "26a5678b-7a2d-5817-8c83-9403924b91f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275827} {:answer/id #uuid "aff51ef5-48b1-5e4e-9bc6-f47b5b3b48de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}+uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277052} {:answer/id #uuid "b6d084df-38e6-570e-8bc2-f410786a2b67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277104} {:answer/id #uuid "c1c454d4-ce80-5860-8edf-68c01e34fae3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{3}-{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1c454d4-ce80-5860-8edf-68c01e34fae3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{3}-{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277198} :answer-field/id #uuid "1900b165-70c5-5f9d-ad38-9a5a829338e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277771}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "92e0422d-8551-525d-a92c-4ab1ea25fb60" :question/math-academy-id "q-161384" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨{z}^{2},\\,{y}^{2},\\,x⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,v,\\,u⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-1,\\,0,\\,2u⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-1,\\,0,\\,2u⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨{z}^{2},\\,{y}^{2},\\,x⟩{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=v\\,z=u} \\\\  & =⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,0,\\,2u⟩ \\\\  & ={u}^{2}\\cdot (-1)+{v}^{2}\\cdot 0+{u}^{2}\\cdot 2u \\\\  & =2{u}^{3}-{u}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,2{u}^{3}-{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421785 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198380 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f322cca7-7530-50bf-b262-89faa81f5906" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Through a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "127c5717-261e-5aef-838e-be5fab62b6d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421765} {:answer/id #uuid "176992fe-e63a-5f75-8661-ee649edc6971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421766} {:answer/id #uuid "794b5eb2-d0f5-57bd-8363-4337b7e59452" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421772} {:answer/id #uuid "cb9f4e2e-e860-55d7-8d5c-c33be0190db3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421778} {:answer/id #uuid "d7fec48c-2c4b-5a3b-8559-e99202ca21e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "127c5717-261e-5aef-838e-be5fab62b6d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421765} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8009739-528a-5b9d-8b7a-977eb7894c6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421781}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f3288098-3c26-556d-b6c9-f206da47adfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-162593" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨3z,\\,-2x,\\,-y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨-v,\\,-u,\\,{u}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-1,\\,2u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2u \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2u \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2u \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-2u,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨3z,\\,-2x,\\,-y⟩|}_{x=-v\\,y=-u\\,z={u}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨3{u}^{2},\\,-2(-v),\\,-(-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{u}^{2},\\,2v,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3{u}^{2},\\,2v,\\,u⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,-2u,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =3{u}^{2}\\cdot 0+2v\\cdot (-2u)+u\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-4uv-u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨3z,\\,-2x,\\,-y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-4uv-u)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-4uv-u)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4uv+u)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[2{u}^{2}v+\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}]}_{u=0}^{u=1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2v+\\frac{1}{2})\\text{d}v \\\\  & =-{[{v}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}v]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
